{"name":"Hint of Orange","hex":"#f8e6d9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hint","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A clue.","An implicit suggestion that avoids a direct statement."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To imply without a direct statement; to provide a clue.","To bring to mind by a slight mention or remote allusion; to suggest in an indirect manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hint"},{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)","wikidata":"Q39338"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg/500px-ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg/1280px-ISS_Expedition_5_crew.jpg?utm_source